<title>USA: ML Direct sees no reason for stock move.</title>
<headline>ML Direct sees no reason for stock move.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>ML Direct Inc said on Thursday it was not aware of any reason for the fluctuation in its stock price.</p>
<p>The company said there was an erroneous wire service report that Sterling Foster &amp; Co had served as an underwriter for ML's stock offering.</p>
<p>It said Sterling Foster had never served an an underwriter for an offering of ML stock.</p>
<p>ML shares began trading on the Nasdaq exchange on September 4.</p>
